issue.body:
The problem is that LazyList gets the entities directly from internally stored entities:

``` java
for (int i = start; i < end; i++) {
    entities.get(i);
}
```

instead of loading them for real:

``` java
for (int i = start; i < end; i++) {
    get(i);
}
```

Authenticator Pro has been renamed to "Stratum".  This can be seen on the [Play Store](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.stratumauth.app&hl=en-US) and the package name also reflects this change as well: `com.stratumauth.app`

When scrolling through the list of apps to import from, new Stratum users might not be familiar with the name change. I suggest renaming the app within the list or at least acknowledging both with something like: Stratum (Auth Pro).


In [app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/importers/AuthenticatorProImporter.java](https://github.com/beemdevelopment/Aegis/blob/a76f3394f3e41dbcf4a706dbdf9b359a0452fd34/app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/importers/AuthenticatorProImporter.java#L48):

```
public class AuthenticatorProImporter extends DatabaseImporter {
    private static final String HEADER = "AUTHENTICATORPRO";
    private static final String HEADER_LEGACY = "AuthenticatorPro";
    private static final String PKG_NAME = "me.jmh.authenticatorpro";
```

