issue.body:
### Livewire version

v4.2.4

### Laravel version

v13.4.0

### PHP version

v8.4.14

### Browser and operating system

Brave on Windows

### Describe the issue you're experiencing

Dynamic event listeners (e.g. `#[On('refresh-children:{parentId}')]`) are not fully supported when a component is marked as `lazy`. Specifically, if the property used in the dynamic event name is set inside `mount()`, this will cause the error `Unable to evaluate dynamic event name placeholder: {parentId}`

### Code snippets to reproduce the issue

**It works** if the child component is not lazy.  
**It works** if `parentId` is set via implicit binding from the parent.
**It does not work** when the property is assigned inside `mount()` — which is required as soon as any logic needs to run before the property is set.

You can try directly here : https://wirebox.app/b/4zw7g

```php
# Parent component
class Simple extends Component
{
    public function render()
    {
        return <<<'BLADE'
            <div
                class="flex w-full flex-col items-center text-gray-300 px-16"
                style="height: 2000px !important"
            >
                <div class="bg-red-600 mb-[1000px]">
                    <button
                        type="button"
                        class="bg-black m-2 p-2 rounded cursor-pointer"
                        wire:click="$dispatch('refresh-children:{{ $this->getId() }}')"
                    >
                        refresh children
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-blue-600 mb-[50px]">
                    <livewire:children
                        :context="[
                            'title' => 'test',
                            'parent_id' => $this->getId(),
                        ]"
                        lazy
                    />
                </div>
            </div>
        BLADE;
    }
}
```
```php
# Children component
<?php
namespace App\Livewire;

use Livewire\Component;
use Livewire\Attributes\On;
use App\Models\SomeData;

class Children extends Component
{
    public string $title;
    public SomeData $someData;
    public string $parentId;

    public function mount(array $context): void
    {
        $this->title = $context['title'] ?? '';
        $this->parentId = $context['parent_id'] ?? '';
    }

    #[On('refresh-children:{parentId}')]
    public function setData(): void
    {
        //
    }

    public function render()
    {
        return <<<'BLADE'
            <div class="flex w-full h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-gray-300 px-16">
                <h1>Title : {{ $title }}</h1>
                <div>Parent Id : {{ $parentId }}</div>
            </div>
        BLADE;
    }
}
```

### Screenshots/screen recordings

Not applicable i guess. Feel free to let me know if you really need to.

### How do you expect it to work?

No error should occur and the dynamic event listener should be triggered correctly, even when the bound property is initialized in mount() and the component is marked as lazy. What do you think about that ?

### Please confirm (incomplete submissions will not be addressed)

